Maintainer: Raydonal Ospina <raydonal@de.ufpe.br>
Description: Partitional clustering of landmark configurations in two or
    three dimensions on Kendall's shape spaces. Provides Partitioning Around
    Medoids (PAM), Ranked K-medoids (Zadegan, Mirzaie and Sadoughi (2013)
    <doi:10.1016/j.knosys.2012.10.012>), Procrustes k-means, CLARANS and
    Hill Climbing with the intrinsic Riemannian or full Procrustes distance,
    and the 'BagClust1' bootstrap ensemble of Dudoit and Fridlyand (2003)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btg038>. Also provides a consensus ensemble
    in tangent principal components (bootstrap k-means, co-association and
    spectral partition), a Gaussian mixture with one variance per cluster
    for groups of unequal spread, an experimental self-attention smoothing,
    the Hopkins test of clustering tendency, simulators for Complex Bingham
    (Kent (1994) <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1994.tb01978.x>) and Gaussian
    landmark data in 2D and 3D, external validation indices (Rand and
    Fowlkes-Mallows), paired Wilcoxon tests, and selection of the number of
    clusters by silhouette width or the gap statistic. Performance-critical
    routines are written in C++ via 'Rcpp' and 'RcppArmadillo'.
